{"id":"fff3236b-7ad7-4a8a-af44-5c67f229eb96","object":"chat.completion","created":1785012934,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"import json\\nfrom collections import Counter\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    \\n    # Build lookup and children mapping\\n    node_by_id = {node['id']: node for node in nodes}\\n    children = {node['id']: [] for node in nodes}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        parent = node['parent']\\n        if parent is not None:\\n            children[parent].append(node['id'])\\n    \\n    # Count occurrences of required symbols\\n    symbol_count = Counter()\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        symbol_count[node['symbol']] += 1\\n    \\n    # Sort nodes by depth descending, then by id ascending\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    \\n    removed_order = []\\n    removed_set = set()\\n    \\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        if not node['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        node_id = node['id']\\n        # Check if any child is still retained\\n        has_retained_child = any(cid not in removed_set for cid in children[node_id])\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        # Check required symbols after tentative removal\\n        temp_counts = symbol_count.copy()\\n        temp_counts[node['symbol']] -= 1\\n        if any(temp_counts[sym] <= 0 for sym in required_symbols):\\n            continue\\n        # Remove node\\n        removed_order.append(node_id)\\n        removed_set.add(node_id)\\n        symbol_count = temp_counts\\n    \\n    retained_ids = [node['id'] for node in nodes if node['id'] not in removed_set]\\n    retained_ids.sort()\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_ids\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for the SE-PE-01 task. The task is about grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree. The input payload has: nodes (list of objects with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility), and required_symbols (list of strings). The goal: reduce the tree by removing nodes that are removable, while preserving required symbols and not breaking grammar (presumably that means the tree remains valid given the parent-child relationships? Actually \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates\" - but from problem statement, we are just doing deletion? And we need to enforce that after removal, all required symbols are still present, and we cannot remove a node that has children that are retained. The method: consider deeper nodes first, use node ID as tiebreaker. We need to return removed_node_ids (list of IDs in order of removal) and retained_node_ids (list of IDs that remain after reduction). The root is always retained (removable=false and required). Also nodes can only be removed if removable=true and their removal does not cause any required symbol to disappear, and they have no children that are retained. We need to decide which removable nodes to actually remove. The problem says: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So we need to simulate removals in order (deepest first, ties broken by ID) and check if after removing that node, the set of symbols present in the tree still includes all required symbols. But also we cannot remove a node that has children that are retained. That suggests we process nodes in a bottom-up order (deeper first), and for each node, if it is removable, check if it can be removed without losing required symbols and if all its children have already been removed (or will be removed? Actually we need to ensure that if we remove a node, its children will also be removed? But the condition says \"never remove a node with retained children\". So we should only remove a node if all its children are removed (or none exist). But we are processing bottom-up, so children are processed before parent; if a child is retained (not removable, or removable but we decided not to remove), then parent cannot be removed. So we need to first decide for each node whether it will be removed, based on removable flag and required symbols check.\n\nThe approach: Build tree from nodes. Identify root (parent null). Determine all nodes that are not removable (including root) must be retained. For removable nodes, we need to consider if we can remove them. The rule: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" That means before removing, check if the symbol of that node is required? Actually the node itself may have a symbol that is required? required_symbols list contains symbols that must appear in the tree. So if a node's symbol is in required_symbols, then removing that node would remove that symbol, unless there is another node with same symbol elsewhere. So we need to check if after removal, the set of symbols from retained nodes (including those not yet removed) still contains all required symbols. Since we process bottom-up, we can accumulate which nodes are removed. But it's easier: iterate nodes in order of decreasing depth (deepest first), and for each removable node, check if it can be removed: \n- Check if any of its children are retained (i.e., not removed yet). If any child is retained, cannot remove (since that would leave child without parent? Actually the child would be orphaned; the tree must stay connected? The problem says \"Never remove a node with retained children\". So we cannot remove a node if it still has children that are retained. So we need to track which nodes are removed.\n- Then check if after removal, the set of symbols from nodes that are not removed (including this node if not removed) still contains all required symbols. But we need to consider that some nodes may be removed later (shallower)? Since we process depth